# BEHAVIORAL ECONOMICS AND FINANCE AT THE HEART OF ADVANCED FINANCIAL AND INVESTMENT DECISION-MAKING SYSTEMS

**Authors:** Vladislav M. Andreev

## Abstract
In recent years, the complexity of decisions that directly affect a person’s well-being (e.g., financial, insurance, medical) has increased. This is why improving the decision-making process is an important task for society. In difficult circumstances, people can greatly benefit from unbiased advice that helps them make more rational decisions in a given area. The move to even more complete automation, facilitated by advances in artificial intelligence, may allow a wide range of consumers to access highly intelligent consulting services at a fairly low price “here and now”, indicating the relevance of understanding the impact of digital consultants and the specifics of their functioning. This article analyzes the work of domestic and foreign authors in the field of using behavioral economics and finance algorithms in various fintech solutions, as well as examples of their application in various startups and at the government level.

